# Changelog

## [v3.3.0] - 2026-10-13

### 🎯 New Features

- **🔗 Compare Link** (`show_compare_link`): Adds a `🔗 View full diff` link to the GitHub compare page below the changelog
  - Disabled by default — set to `"true"` to enable

- **✂️ Limit Listed Commits** (`max_commits`): Lists only the N most recent commits and summarizes the rest as `…and N more commit(s)` with a link to the full diff
  - Empty (default) or `0` shows all commits, exactly as before

- **📅 Changelog Fallback** (`since_ref`): When there is no previous successful run (for example the first run on a branch), the changelog now starts from `since_ref` (tag, branch or SHA), or covers the **last 30 days** when `since_ref` is not set
  - Previously the first run had no changelog at all
  - "Last Deploy" in statistics is only shown when the range starts at a previous run

- **🚦 Explicit Status Handling** (`notify_on_cancel`): Cancelled runs get their own message (`⚠️ … was cancelled.`) instead of a success-style deployment message
  - Disabled by default — set `notify_on_cancel: "true"` and pass `workflow_status: ${{ job.status }}`
  - Failure and cancelled messages now include the run duration and can be previewed with `test_mode`

- **🎨 Environment Emoji Map** (`environment_emojis`): Map branch globs to emojis, one `<glob>=<emoji>` per line (case-insensitive, first match wins). Falls back to `staging_emoji` / `production_emoji`

- **📤 Action Outputs**: `message_id`, `message`, `commit_count`, `previous_sha`, `compare_url` for use in later workflow steps

- **🔁 Retry with Backoff**: Network errors, HTTP 429 and HTTP 5xx from ClickUp are retried up to 3 times with exponential backoff (honors `Retry-After`)

### 🐛 Bug Fixes

- **Test mode left temporary files behind**: a trailing `\` turned the cleanup command into arguments of the preview script
- **Backslashes in commit messages, titles and descriptions were interpreted** (`\t`, `\n`, `\c`…) because messages were printed with `echo -e`; content is now sent verbatim
- **Copilot agent attribution** used the first `Co-authored-by` found in *any* commit; it now uses the commit's own co-author, falling back to another Copilot commit's co-author
- **Breaking-change marker dropped**: `refactor!: …` was rendered as `**Refactor:**`; it is now `**Refactor!:**`
- **Duration was always `unknown` on macOS runners**: timestamps are now parsed with `jq` instead of GNU `date -d`
- **Co-author names with an apostrophe** (e.g. `O'Brien`) could abort commit processing
- **Statistics** no longer print `integer expression expected` errors when a count is zero; fix/feat/refactor counts include breaking variants (`fix!:`)
- **Workspace names** resolved in test mode are sanitized before being loaded by the preview script

### 🔒 Security

- Inputs are passed to scripts through `env:` instead of being pasted into shell code, so quotes or `$(...)` in `title`/`description` can no longer break or alter the scripts
- `GITHUB_TOKEN` and other values are no longer exported to `$GITHUB_ENV` (they leaked into later steps of the calling job)
- The ClickUp API token is passed to `curl` through a header file instead of command-line arguments

### 🧪 Quality

- Added a `bats` unit test suite (`tests/`) and a CI workflow running ShellCheck, actionlint and the tests on pull requests
- The staging test workflow now runs the sub-actions from the checked-out branch instead of the last published tag, and previews failure/cancelled messages and new options
- Added `.gitattributes` to keep LF line endings for scripts and YAML

### ⚠️ Behaviour Changes

- With `if: always()`, a **cancelled** run no longer sends the normal deployment message. Set `notify_on_cancel: "true"` to get a cancellation message
- Environment variables `CLICKUP_WORKSPACE_ID`, `CLICKUP_PROJECT_NAME`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `REPO_NAME`, `TRIGGERING_ACTOR`, `STAGING_EMOJI` and `PRODUCTION_EMOJI` are no longer added to the calling job's environment
- The first run on a branch now shows commits from the last 30 days (or since `since_ref`) instead of no changelog

### 📝 Migration Guide

No input was removed or renamed. To adopt the new features:

```yaml
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v3.3.0
  id: clickup
  if: always()
  with:
    # ... existing inputs ...
    show_compare_link: "true"      # 🔗 View full diff
    max_commits: "20"              # list the 20 most recent commits
    since_ref: "v1.0.0"            # first-run fallback (default: last 30 days)
    notify_on_failure: "true"
    notify_on_cancel: "true"
    workflow_status: ${{ job.status }}
    environment_emojis: |
      release/beta=🅱️
      *hotfix*=🔥

- run: echo "Sent ClickUp message ${{ steps.clickup.outputs.message_id }}"
```

---

## [v3.2.0] - 2026-05-11

### 🎯 New Features

- **🤖 Agent Commit Filtering** (`filter_agent_commits`): Automatically filters out agent-generated commits (e.g., "Initial plan", "Agent-Logs-Url:", "Co-authored-by:") from the changelog for cleaner notifications
  - Enabled by default — set to `"false"` to show all commits
  - Also strips `Co-authored-by:` trailer lines from commit message bodies

- **🔤 Capitalized Contributor Names**: All contributor names are now displayed in Title Case for consistent formatting
  - `copilot swe agent bot` → `Copilot Swe Agent Bot`
  - `contributor name` → `Contributor Name`

- **🤝 Copilot Agent Attribution**: When the commit author is "copilot swe agent bot", the action extracts the co-authored contributor name and displays it as `"Real Name (Copilot Agent)"` instead of the bot name
  - Example: `ContributorName (Copilot Agent)` instead of `Copilot Swe Agent Bot`

- **🎨 Environment-Specific Emojis** (`staging_emoji`, `production_emoji`): Customize the notification emoji per environment
  - Staging branches default to 🧪, production branches default to 🚀
  - Auto-detected based on branch name containing "staging"

- **📂 Group Commits by Type** (`group_commits_by_type`): Group changelog entries by conventional commit type (Features, Fixes, Refactors, etc.) instead of by author
  - Disabled by default — set to `"true"` to enable
  - Automatically maps commit types to labeled categories with emojis
  - Strips redundant type prefix from commit messages under type headers

- **🔗 PR Link Association** (`show_pr_links`): Automatically linkifies `#123` PR/issue references in commit messages to GitHub pull request URLs
  - Disabled by default — set to `"true"` to enable

- **❌ Failure Notifications** (`notify_on_failure`, `workflow_status`): Send a notification when the workflow fails, including the triggering user, project name, branch, and a direct link to the workflow run
  - Disabled by default — set `notify_on_failure: "true"` and pass `workflow_status: ${{ job.status }}`
  - Use `if: always()` on the action step to ensure it runs on failure

### 🧹 Improvements

- **📊 Capitalized Statistics Names**: Top contributor name in statistics is now Title Cased and Copilot agent bot names are displayed as "Copilot Agent"

### 📝 Migration Guide

All new features are backwards compatible. Existing workflows will continue to work without changes.

To adopt new features:

```yaml
# v3.2.0 with all new features
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v3.2.0
  if: always() # Required for failure notifications
  with:
    # ... existing inputs ...
    filter_agent_commits: "true"        # Filter bot commits (default)
    group_commits_by_type: "false"      # Group by author (default)
    show_pr_links: "false"             # Disable PR links (default)
    staging_emoji: "🧪"                # Custom staging emoji
    production_emoji: "🚀"             # Custom production emoji
    notify_on_failure: "true"          # Enable failure notifications
    workflow_status: ${{ job.status }}  # Pass job status
```

---

## [v3.1.0] - 2025-10-22

### 🎯 Enhanced Features

- **🔤 Case-Insensitive Conventional Commits**: Conventional commit types now accept any case (lowercase, UPPERCASE, Capitalize) and automatically normalize to capitalized format
  - `feat`, `FEAT`, `Feat` all become `**Feat:**`
  - `fix`, `FIX`, `Fix` all become `**Fix:**`
  - Works with all conventional commit types: build, chore, docs, feat, fix, refactor, revert, style, test, release, security, deps, api

### 🧹 Improvements

- **📊 Smarter Statistics Display**: Enhanced conditional visibility for cleaner stats
  - Hide "Release Type" when it's "Other" (non-conventional commits)
  - Hide "Last Deploy" if time difference is less than 30 minutes
  - Hide "Contributor(s)" count if less than 2 contributors
  - Hide "Top Contributor" if less than 3 contributors
  - Only show relevant metrics to reduce noise

### 🗑️ Removed Features

- **❌ Removed Alphabetical Sorting**: Eliminated `sort_commits_alphabetically` feature
  - Commits now display in chronological order (as committed)
  - Removed complex sorting logic that caused commit title/description separation issues
  - Simplified codebase by removing problematic sorting functionality
  - Breaking change: `sort_commits_alphabetically` input parameter no longer available

### 🐛 Bug Fixes

- **✅ Fixed Commit Block Integrity**: Resolved issue where multi-line commits were being separated during processing
- **🔧 Cleaner Code**: Removed unused sorting logic and simplified commit processing pipeline

### ⚠️ Breaking Changes

- Removed `sort_commits_alphabetically` input parameter from action and all sub-actions
- Commits will always appear in chronological order

### 📝 Migration Guide

If you were using `sort_commits_alphabetically: "true"`:

```yaml
# Before (v3.0.0)
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v3.0.0
  with:
    sort_commits_alphabetically: "true" # ❌ No longer available

# After (v3.1.0)
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v3.1.0
  with:
    # ✅ Remove sort_commits_alphabetically parameter
    # Commits will display chronologically
```

---

## [v3.0.0] - 2025-06-19

### 🚀 Major Features

- **📊 Commit Statistics**: Display detailed deployment metrics including commits, files changed, lines added/removed, contributors, and time since last deployment
- **🧪 Test Mode**: Preview notifications without sending to ClickUp, with workspace/channel name resolution
- **📝 Enhanced Commit Processing**: Improved commit sorting (A-Z), merge commit filtering, and message formatting
- **🏗️ Modular Architecture**: Complete refactoring into script-based components for better maintainability

### 🎯 New Input Parameters

- `show_commit_statistics`: Display commit statistics table (default: "false")
- `test_mode`: Preview mode without sending to ClickUp (default: "false")
- `sort_commits_alphabetically`: Sort commits A-Z by message (default: "true")
- `full_commit_message`: Use full commit message vs first line only (default: "true")

### 🔧 Technical Improvements

- **Scripts-Based Architecture**: Split large actions into focused, reusable scripts
  - `fetch-commits`: 5 specialized scripts for commit processing
  - `send-notification`: 5 specialized scripts for message handling
- **Helper Functions**: Added `format_task_links()` and `format_conventional_commit()` functions
- **Name Resolution**: Automatically resolve workspace and channel IDs to human-readable names
- **Enhanced Error Handling**: Improved validation and error reporting
- **Better Separation of Concerns**: Each script handles a single responsibility
- **Enhanced Link Format**: Changed task links from `[\`ID\`]`to`[***ID***]` for better cross-platform compatibility

### 🐛 Bug Fixes

- **🔗 ClickUp Desktop App Compatibility**: Fixed task link formatting issue where backticks in link text caused problems with ClickUp desktop app while maintaining perfect web compatibility
- **🧹 Code Refactoring**: Eliminated code duplication in commit processing by extracting helper functions for task link formatting and conventional commit handling
- **📝 Improved Maintainability**: Consolidated duplicate regex patterns and sed commands into reusable functions

### 📊 Commit Statistics Features

- **📝 Total Commits**: Count of commits in deployment
- **📁 Files Changed**: Number of modified files
- **➕➖ Lines**: Added and removed lines of code
- **👥 Contributors**: Number of unique commit authors
- **⏰ Time Since Last Deploy**: Human-readable time difference
- **📋 Table Format**: Clean vertical table layout

### 🧪 Test Mode Features

- **🔍 Message Preview**: See exact content before sending
- **📝 Metadata Display**: Character count, format, destination details
- **🏷️ Name Resolution**: Show workspace and channel names (not just IDs)
- **🔒 Security**: API token hidden in preview
- **📋 Clear Instructions**: How to switch to live mode

### 🏗️ Architecture Changes

- **Modular Scripts**: Each component split into focused shell scripts
- **Better Maintainability**: Easier to debug, test, and modify individual components
- **Improved Reusability**: Scripts can be used independently or in other contexts
- **Cleaner Codebase**: Reduced complexity in main action files

### ⚡ Performance & Quality

- **Conditional Processing**: Statistics and name resolution only run when needed
- **Efficient API Calls**: Optimized ClickUp API usage
- **Better Error Recovery**: Graceful fallbacks for API failures
- **Improved Logging**: Better visibility into action execution

### 🔄 Migration Guide from v2.x

**✅ No Breaking Changes** - v3.0.0 is fully backward compatible with v2.x configurations.

**New Optional Parameters:**

- All new parameters have sensible defaults and are optional
- Existing workflows will continue to work without modification
- New features are opt-in via new input parameters

**Recommended Updates:**

```yaml
# Update version reference
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v3.0.0
  with:
    # ... existing inputs work as-is ...

    # Optional: Enable new features
    show_commit_statistics: "true" # Add deployment metrics
    test_mode: "false" # Preview during development
    sort_commits_alphabetically: "true" # Already default
```

**No Action Required:**

- ✅ Existing secrets work unchanged
- ✅ All input parameters remain compatible
- ✅ Output format is consistent (unless new features enabled)
- ✅ No workflow file changes needed for basic functionality

**Safe Upgrade Testing:**

```yaml
# Test the upgrade safely before going live
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v3.0.0
  with:
    # ... your existing configuration ...
    test_mode: "true" # Preview changes without sending
```

## [v2.0.1] - 2025-06-15

### 🚨 Critical Bug Fix

- **Fixed Path Resolution Issue**: Replaced relative step paths (`./steps/`) with full repository paths (`architweb/ClickUpNotification/steps/`) to prevent "Can't find action.yml" errors when used from external repositories

## [v2.0.0] - 2025-06-15

### 🚀 Major Features

- **Modular Architecture**: Complete refactoring into separate, reusable steps
  - `⏱️ Fetch Duration` step for workflow time tracking
  - `📝 Fetch Commits` step for changelog generation
  - `📢 Send ClickUp Notification` step for message delivery
- **Custom Title Support**: Add custom titles to override default deployment message
- **Custom Description Support**: Add italic descriptions below the main message
- **Configurable Components**: Independently enable/disable duration and changelog features

### 🎨 Enhanced Message Format

- **Smart Title Logic**: Custom title shows as "🚀 **branch** | **project** | **title**"
- **Flexible Description**: Optional italic description positioned after deploy info
- **Improved Message Flow**: Better structured notifications with consistent formatting

### ⚙️ New Input Parameters

- `title`: Custom title for notification messages (default: "")
- `description`: Custom description displayed in italics (default: "")
- `show_fetch_duration`: Control duration display (default: "true")
- `show_changelog_commits`: Control changelog display (default: "true")

### 🔧 Technical Improvements

- **Better Error Handling**: Improved variable references and error checking
- **Cleaner Code**: Separated concerns for better maintainability
- **Independent Testing**: Each step can be tested and debugged separately
- **Reusable Components**: Steps can be used in other workflows

### 📋 Migration Guide

Update your workflows to use `v2.0.1` and optionally add new parameters:

```yaml
- uses: architweb/ClickUpNotification@v2.0.1
  with:
    # ... existing required parameters ...
    # New optional parameters:
    title: "🎉 Production Release"
    description: "Major feature update deployed"
    show_fetch_duration: "true"
    show_changelog_commits: "true"
```

---

## [v1.5.0] - 2025-05-31

### Added

- Added support for custom task IDs.
- Added support for multiple IDs.
- Added the option to use the full commit message.
- Added parsing of Conventional Commit types.

### Changed

- Fixed minor syntax bug.

## [v1.4.2] - 2025-05-28

### Added

- Added support for running the workflow on macOS.

### Changed

- Changed commit message keyword for task ID detection from "task-id:" to "task:".

## [v1.4.0] - 2025-05-13

### Added

- Added automatic ClickUp task link creation from commit messages
- Added support for detecting task IDs in format `task-id: \`TASK_ID\`` in commit messages
- Added conversion of task IDs to clickable links in notification messages
- Support for alphanumeric task IDs (like "86eqv0y92")
- Enhanced message formatting to show task ID as clickable link with pipe separator format

## [v1.3.0] - 2025-05-13

### Improved

- Added sanitization for author names to handle special characters and symbols.
- Replaced problematic characters in commit author names with spaces.
- Added fallback to "Unknown Contributor" when author name becomes empty after sanitization.
- Cleaned up unnecessary comments and debug statements from all steps:
  - Removed redundant logging from "Fetch Duration" step
  - Removed unnecessary debug output from "Fetch Commits" step
  - Streamlined "Send ClickUp Notification" step
- Optimized overall workflow execution by reducing verbose output.

## [v1.2.0] - 2025-05-05

### Added

- Initial release of **ClickUpNotification** GitHub Action.
- Fetches commits between the last successful CI/CD run and the current run.
- Sends a formatted notification to ClickUp with commit messages and authors.
- Duration of the CI/CD process included in the notification.
